@@ -1491,3 +1491,37 @@ TP>1 retains the ordinary activation and RowParallelLinear reduction.
 The fusion preserves the unfused CUDA activation and MXFP8 bytes. No FastH3
 adapter, AdaLN sidecar, fixed sampling schedule, or SP8 layout is required.
 Runtime adapter switching after conversion is not qualified by this recipe.
+
+### Optional video VAE optimizations
+
+Enable video decoder MXFP8 separately from DiT quantization:
+
+```bash
+--diffusion-quantization-config '{"transformer":null,"text_encoder":null,"video_vae":{"method":"mxfp8"},"audio_vae":null}'
+```
+
+This approximate mode quantizes the decoder's QKV, attention output and two MLP
+weights directly from the FP32 checkpoint. Residuals, normalization, encoder,
+convolutions and audio VAE keep their existing precision. Activations use the
+existing FP16 decode boundary; `ignored_layers` can exempt decoder projections.
+A global quantization setting does not implicitly select VAE quantization.
+
+For the canonical 1280x704, 362-frame decode (latent `[1,24,107,44,80]`),
+`VLLM_OMNI_H3_VAE_BATCHING=paired` balances spatial tiles across pairs of temporal
+windows. `mixed` additionally batches local tile decodes at batch sizes 4/2/1 (a three-tile
+tail splits into 2+1 to avoid the observed FP16 batch-three drift), preserving
+attention-output projection calls at their original batch-one geometry. Both
+require native distributed VAE tiling and reject incompatible geometry. The
+normal decode and chunk-consumer APIs share this path. Other geometries continue
+to use the default implementation when this option is unset.
+
+`VLLM_OMNI_H3_VAE_GATHER_OVERLAP=1` submits paired gathers on a separate stream.
+It requires nonblocking NCCL; all communication and output streams drain before
+return or error propagation. Only the output rank allocates receive storage.
+`VLLM_OMNI_H3_VAE_AUDIO_OVERLAP=1` overlaps audio with the complete video decode
+on CUDA while keeping both residency contexts alive. It increases concurrent
+memory use and does not alter the audio-first chunked MP4 mux path.
+
+These options are independent and disabled by default. Batch scheduling and
+stream overlap require their own output comparison; MXFP8 is approximate even
+when the scheduling operations preserve the reference ordering.
